2. Parameter types and multiple return values
Positional parameters are matched by order; keyword parameters are matched by name and improve clarity; default
parameters make an argument optional. A function can return multiple values as a tuple, for example return total, gst. The
caller can unpack them using total, gst = calculate_bill(...).
def calculate_bill(amount, gst_rate=0.05):
    gst = amount * gst_rate
    total = amount + gst
    return total, gst
